Subject: [PATCH 24/24] Seamless cells: no loading screen, and doors walked through

With [Cells] seamless cells (Alpha3::seamlessCells) a cell change after the first goes without the fade and the
loading screen: Scene takes a quiet loading listener for the cell grid, the terrain preload and the interior load.

With [Cells] seamless doors (Alpha3::seamlessDoors) the player activating a door between an exterior and an interior
(either way, or between interiors) opens it (MWWorld::SeamlessDoors, mwworld/seamlessdoors.cpp): the door's model
swings open and the other side is drawn through the doorway (Alpha3::makeDoorPortal, support/src/doorportal.cpp),
placed so that the door there sits on this one: the interior's objects, or the exterior's objects and terrain (the
terrain's chunk manager, now reachable) lit by the weather outside (weather.cpp tells Alpha3 while in an interior).
The player walks through the doorway: mwphysics' actor sweeps and unstuck let the door and the wall in it through
(Alpha3::doorwayPassable). Crossing it they are in the other cell at the same place and heading, the door there open
behind them.
